    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The fire in the brazier is dying... just like everything else. I can still hear them. The men. The sound of the river turning red because I couldn't read the scouts' reports. I sat there in the command tent while they were butchered because of my pride. I’m not a commander anymore. I’m just a ghost waiting for the world to realize I should have died on that field with them. There is no honor left in this skin.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
